        "item/files-versions-replace"
      ],
      "doneWhen": "Every FilePolicy ability states its posture on a file trashed on its own in a LIVE directory, rather than three postures existing by accident: replace() refuses, update()/move()/legalHold() do not, and delete()/restore()/purge() deliberately must not. update(), move() and legalHold() refuse a trashed file; a FilePolicyTest case covers each; each carries a mutations.json entry. The reachability question is SETTLED rather than assumed -- a Livewire::test() case selects a file, trashes it out of band, calls renameFile() and asserts WHICH guard refused (403 from the policy, not 404 from a scoped restoration query), so the verdict says whether Livewire's restoration applies the SoftDeletingScope; that answer is recorded either way, because it is the same fact replace()'s guard rests on.",
      "actionStatus": "CompletedActionStatus",
      "startTime": "2026-09-18T00:47:00Z",
