    {
      "@id": "item/email-verification-decided",
      "@type": "Action",
      "order": 39,
      "name": "Email verification either enforces something or stops claiming to",
      "url": "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/issues/161",
      "isBasedOn": [
        "spec:10-user-facing-surface"
      ],
      "size": "S",
      "release": "v1.0.0",
      "dependsOn": [],
      "doneWhen": "An unverified user's treatment is DECIDED and enforced, and a test asserts it. Today config/fortify.php enables Features::emailVerification(), the dashboard route carries the `verified` middleware, and four EmailVerificationTest tests pass -- while nothing is gated, because User extends Illuminate\\Foundation\\Auth\\User (which supplies the MustVerifyEmail TRAIT) but declares only `implements PasskeyUser`, and EnsureEmailIsVerified gates on the CONTRACT. The instanceof is false, so every unverified user passes straight through the one route that guards on it. Either route is acceptable: implement the contract and apply `verified` consistently, or remove Features::emailVerification() and the middleware so nothing claims a guarantee the system does not make. What is NOT acceptable is leaving the present shape, where the guard reads as protection and enforces nothing. The test asserting an unverified user's treatment is mutation-checked. The existing four pass with the guard doing nothing, which is exactly what a mutation would have caught and is why this went unnoticed. If verification stays, the no-mailer case is answered rather than assumed: a fresh container configures no mailer, so implementing the contract would redirect a newly registered user -- including the installer's first administrator -- to a notice they can never satisfy, locking them out of their own instance on first boot. The container smoke proves the first admin still reaches the app. The route inconsistency is settled in the same pass: files.browse, files.download, search and admin.* carry `auth` alone where dashboard carries `auth` + `verified`.",
      "actionStatus": "CompletedActionStatus",
      "startTime": "2026-09-18T11:25:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-09-18T12:01:36Z",
      "result": [
        "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/pull/195"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "item/extraction-missing-object",
      "@type": "Action",
      "order": 40,
      "name": "A missing object is distinguishable on the extraction path too",
      "url": "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/issues/153",
      "isBasedOn": [
        "spec:7-text-extraction"
      ],
      "size": "S",
      "release": "v1.0.0",
      "dependsOn": [
        "item/download-missing-object"
      ],
      "doneWhen": "DocumentStorage::downloadToTemp() throws the typed ObjectMissingFromStorage rather than a bare RuntimeException, so a caller can tell \"the row exists but the bytes are gone\" from any other storage failure -- the distinction item/download-missing-object made on the two download routes, applied to the path ExtractText actually uses. AND what the queue does with it is asserted rather than inherited: whether the job stops retrying against bytes that are never coming back, and what file_texts.status an operator can read afterwards. The failure mode here is not a bad HTTP status but a queue that may never settle, which is less visible than issue #134 was and harder to diagnose. The test queue is synchronous and production's is not, so any assertion about retry or backoff must be written to hold in production rather than only in the suite.",
      "actionStatus": "CompletedActionStatus",
      "startTime": "2026-09-18T12:47:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-09-18T13:11:14Z",
      "result": [
        "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/pull/200"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "item/ledger-main-push-record",
      "@type": "Action",
      "order": 41,
      "name": "Every push to main is recorded per run, and CI can prove none is missing",
      "url": "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/issues/172",
      "isBasedOn": [
        "spec:13-infrastructure"
      ],
      "size": "M",
      "release": "v1.0.0",
      "dependsOn": [
        "item/ledger-mutation-nodes"
      ],
      "doneWhen": "A Run records every push to main in its window, not only those carrying a PullRequest node. runErrors() iterates `pullRequests`, and ledger-only PRs have no node at all, so the rule speaks for 3 of run/0019's 8 merges -- and the uncovered class has the worse record, since BOTH times main has gone red it was a ledger-only merge (9e2f7af, fixed by #158; 6663282, fixed by #138). Shape: `Run.merges`, a list of {mergeSha, pullRequest|null, mergedAt, testsRun, testsConclusion, ledgerRun, ledgerConclusion}. Two NAMED workflow fields rather than a list, because LOOP step 3 names exactly `tests` and `ledger` and those are the whole of what a main push triggers, so a closed pair cannot under-report where a list is only as complete as its caller. mainRunUrl/mainConclusion move off PullRequest so the fact has one home. Rules, each mutation-checked: every merged PullRequest's mergeSha appears in its mergedIn run's merges, which catches an item PR omitted from the list; Run.commit is DEFINED as the last entry's mergeSha; and outcome completed requires the last entry's conclusions to be success, so \"run/0018 closes green\" stops being prose and becomes checked. And the clause without which this is only bookkeeping: omission is detectable only against an external list. ledger.yml checks out at the default fetch-depth 1; at fetch-depth 0 the CLI wrapper hands the validator `git log --first-parent <previous completed run's commit>..HEAD` and the validator asserts every sha appears in some Run.merges. LedgerValidator stays framework-free and file-only -- the WRAPPER supplies the git fact, the two-caller seam its docblock already describes. No node-shaped fix substitutes for this: whatever type is added, the validator iterates nodes that exist, and a merge nobody wrote down stays invisible.",
      "actionStatus": "CompletedActionStatus",
      "startTime": "2026-09-18T13:45:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-09-18T14:06:39Z",
      "result": [
        "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/pull/203"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "item/ledger-field-audit",
      "@type": "Action",
      "order": 42,
      "name": "Three ledger fields read as evidence and record nothing: enforce each or delete it",
      "url": "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/issues/173",
      "isBasedOn": [
        "spec:13-infrastructure"
      ],
      "size": "S",
      "release": "v1.0.0",
      "dependsOn": [
        "item/ledger-main-push-record"
      ],
      "doneWhen": "Decision.evidence is populated on 0 of 43 decisions and its resolveEach branch has never run on real data -- the state decision/0043 just corrected one node type over. decision/0038 argued the absence would itself be a signal, but a signal absent in 100% of cases carries none, and decisions 0038/0040/0042 each rest on a specific mutation verdict without citing it. Either require it on a Decision whose `affects` names an item carrying a Mutation node in the same run, or delete the key. Run.tests and Run.assertions are copied forward rather than measured: run/0016 and run/0017 both report 649/1340 across a run that merged three items, and run/0019 carried run/0018's 701/1446 while merging three more. Either read them from the recorded main run, which item/ledger-main-push-record makes available, or remove them -- and either give -1 the stated meaning \"not measured\" or abolish it. Run.commit has no stated semantics beyond a sha shape and is inconsistent: every run's is its last substantive merge EXCEPT run/0017, whose dbf7ce7 is the #123 merge that closed run/0016 -- main at run/0017's start, equal to its startTime rather than to its work. Each resolution is mutation-checked: deleting the enforcement reddens a named test. A field that is DELETED needs no test, since its absence from ALLOWED_KEYS is the assertion and LedgerIntegrityTest already fails an unknown key.",
      "actionStatus": "CompletedActionStatus",
      "startTime": "2026-09-18T14:20:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-09-18T14:35:03Z",
      "result": [
        "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/pull/205"
      ]
    },
    {
