    {
      "@id": "item/spec-reconcile",
      "@type": "Action",
      "order": 52,
      "name": "Reconcile the spec with what actually shipped, before the audit reads it",
      "url": "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/issues/219",
      "isBasedOn": [
        "spec:12-documentation"
      ],
      "size": "S",
      "release": "v1.0.0",
      "dependsOn": [],
      "doneWhen": "The spec is both the standard item/v1-audit measures against and the text workers are briefed with (LOOP.md step 5 hands a worker 'the relevant spec section'), and it has drifted from the product in three verified places: line 1025 names base image 8.4 where the Dockerfile is 8.5; the section 2 decision table still says search ships on Laravel Scout's database driver, which is not installed -- search goes through the SearchIndex seam, and line 426 of the SAME document already says so, so the spec contradicts itself and section 2 is the half read first; line 1135 lists SQLite FTS5 as a post-v1 optimisation though Fts5SearchIndex has shipped and line 438 describes it. .github/workflows/ledger.yml pinning php-version 8.4 is the same staleness one file over. Done when each is corrected or explicitly marked superseded with a pointer to the section that now governs, the section 2 / section 8 contradiction is resolved in one direction, a dated revisions note at the top says what was reconciled, ledger.yml runs 8.5, and validate-ledger.php still passes -- which is what proves no heading moved. TWO CONSTRAINTS. Spec headings are load-bearing: LedgerValidator's spec-anchor rule derives valid isBasedOn anchors from them, so a renamed or removed heading reddens ledger.yml; edit content only. And section 2 is a decision table cited by decisions 0001 through 0004, so a superseded row is MARKED superseded rather than deleted -- the spec is a design record, and a row that silently changes loses why the original choice was made. This is deliberately NOT folded into item/v1-audit: see decision/0077.",
      "actionStatus": "PotentialActionStatus",
      "startTime": null,
      "endTime": null,
      "result": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "item/api-sanctum-tokens",
      "@type": "Action",
      "order": 53,
      "name": "Sanctum tokens managed from My Account",
      "url": "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/issues/22",
