      "endTime": null,
      "result": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "item/api-content",
      "@type": "Action",
      "order": 54,
      "name": "The /api/v1 content surface",
      "url": "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/issues/23",
      "isBasedOn": [
        "spec:11-api"
      ],
      "size": "L",
      "release": "v1.0.0",
      "dependsOn": [
        "item/api-sanctum-tokens",
        "item/content-actions",
        "item/search-filters",
        "item/trash-directory"
      ],
      "doneWhen": "Per-endpoint three-gate matrix: a missing ability is 403 despite the permission, a denied ACL is 404 or 403, and revoking the owner's role narrows an existing token on the next request; a test asserts no /api route touches users, roles, definition writes or periods. The 404-or-403 choice this clause left open is settled as 404, and settled ONCE for the whole product: a denied ACL answers 404, the same as a nonexistent id, on every route AND in Browser::moveFile()/moveDirectory(), whose destination lookup is scoped to DirectoryAccess::viewableDirectoryIds() inside the query rather than resolved with findOrFail before authorize (issue #109). The two existing tests asserting 403 flip to 404 in the same PR. Deciding it here rather than ad hoc in the Livewire component is the point: two postures in one product is the cost of deciding it twice.",
      "actionStatus": "PotentialActionStatus",
      "startTime": null,
      "endTime": null,
      "result": []
    },
    {
      "@id": "item/api-presigned-upload",
      "@type": "Action",
      "order": 55,
      "name": "Presigned upload, commit and the staging sweep",
      "url": "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/issues/24",
      "isBasedOn": [
        "spec:11-api"
      ],
      "size": "M",
      "release": "v1.0.0",
      "dependsOn": [
        "item/api-content"
      ],
      "doneWhen": "End-to-end url then commit; a size or checksum mismatch is rejected and the staging object removed; an archived period is rejected at upload-url; the sweep removes only stale staging objects. The per-file versions commit appends through a StoreFileVersion entry point taking the File itself, which cannot create one (issue #115): the API commit step has no Directory and no client filename, so it cannot use handle() without the string-passing hazard that issue describes. Browser::replaceFile() moves onto the same entry point. handle()'s create-or-append behaviour and StoreFileVersionTest are unchanged, and the container smoke's replace mutation (PR #118) still fails against an image whose Replace calls handle() with the client filename.",
